{"name":"Okra","hex":"#3e912d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"okra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The edible immature mucilaginous seed pod (properly, capsule) of the Abelmoschus esculentus.","The flowering mallow plant Abelmoschus esculentus itself, now commonly grown in the tropics and warmer parts of the temperate zones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/okra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Okra","blocks":[{"text":"Okra, Abelmoschus esculentus, known in some English-speaking countries as lady's fingers, is a flowering plant in the mallow family native to West Africa. Cultivated in tropical, subtropical, and warm temperate regions around the world for its edible green seed pods, okra is used in the cuisines of many countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Hong_Kong_Okra_Aug_25_2012.JPG/330px-Hong_Kong_Okra_Aug_25_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okra","wikidata":"Q80531"},{"title":"Okra (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Okra\" is a song by American hip hop artist Tyler, the Creator, released as a digital single on March 29, 2018. It was written and produced by Tyler, the Creator. Described by Tyler as a \"throwaway song\", the single garnered media attention for its abrupt release and a lyrical reference to American actor Timothée Chalamet. \"Okra\" has been described as a rap song with bass, drums, snare, piano, and strings in its instrumentation, with its production complementing Tyler's vocal performance, which was shifted up one semitone. In the lyrics, Tyler makes references to several pop culture figures in addition to Chalamet, and also alludes to the separation of hip hop collective Odd Future, which Tyler co-founded."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/OKRA_Tyler%2C_the_Creator.svg/330px-OKRA_Tyler%2C_the_Creator.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okra_(song)","wikidata":"Q52160873"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG/500px-Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG/1280px-Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG/500px-Okra%28Abelmoschus_esculentus%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whole plant with blossom and immature pod","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOkra(Abelmoschus_esculentus).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg/500px-Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg/1280px-Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg/500px-Ladies%27_Finger_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Longitudinal section of fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALadies'_Finger_BNC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Giant_okra.jpg/120px-Giant_okra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Giant_okra.jpg/250px-Giant_okra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Giant_okra.j